    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **264 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**. BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection to match the new specification.\n\n### Behavior changes\n- **New identity key**: `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`. The `householdId` is no longer part of the key.\n- **Duplicate detection (409)** is now the single identity key, still ignoring soft-deleted owners and still applying the disposable-email-domain blocklist first (that check lives earlier in the pipeline, in `NormalizeOwnerEmail`).\n- **Soft match** now triggers when the identity key differs but `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match (previously it keyed off exact last name + different telephone).\n- **Household 409 block removed**: two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones now have different keys, so they are created as a soft match rather than rejected. The separate `householdId`-based 409 no longer applies.\n\n### Changes made\n- `model/Soundex.java` *(new)* \u2014 dependency-free classic American Soundex encoder, shared by the key and the soft-match check.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 `getIdentityKey()` now returns the SHA-256 hex over telephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName); added a private `sha256Hex` helper and imports.\n- `function/owner/AssignPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 soft match now on `soundex(lastName)` + postcode, guarded so an exact identity match isn't double-counted.\n- `function/owner/EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique.java` \u2014 javadoc updated (logic already keyed off `getIdentityKey()`).\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 removed the `ensureHouseholdUnique` step; `assignHousehold` now flows straight to `ensureIdentityUnique`.\n- Deleted the now-dead `EnsureHouseholdUnique`, `DuplicateHouseholdException`, `DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler`, and its escalation YAML; fixed dangling javadoc links in `AssignHouseholdId` and `DeleteOwner`.\n- `AssignHouseholdId` is retained (it still populates `householdId`, which the response and `sharesHousehold` flow use).\n\n### Test change\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests` \u2014 the old `createOwnerRejectsHouseholdDuplicate` test asserted the now-removed household 409. Replaced it with `createOwnerAllowsHouseholdSoftMatchWithDifferentTelephone`, which asserts the second owner is created (201) and flagged `possibleDuplicate: true` / `possibleDuplicateOf` the first. The existing `AcceptanceTest` identity-key-v2 cases (64-hex shape and identity collision \u2192 409) pass unchanged.",
